  "source": {
    "path": "sources/treasury-mts/mts-202605.pdf",
    "table": "Table 5. Outlays of the U.S. Government, May 2026 and Other Periods",
    "page": 15,
    "title": "Department of Justice section (Table-5 cap-fit unit, page 15). Full 9-column outlays model. Reclassified from over-cap to cap-fit by the 2026-07-15 sizing pass (120 cells at the cap; the earlier 123 estimate was over-cap by rounding). FLAT section: 'Legal Activities and U.S. Marshals' and 'Office of Justice Programs' are visual groupings with NO printed subtotals, so every line feeds Total--Department of Justice directly (like -commerce). Family pattern: plans/treasury-mts-2026-05-outlays-table5.md; worked examples: -commerce (flat), -legislative.",
    "period": "May FY2026 (This Month = May 2026; Current FYTD = Oct 2025 - May 2026; Prior FYTD = Oct 2024 - May 2025)"
  },
  "unit_note": "USD millions ('[$ millions]' per table header). Table 5 legend (p. 23): '......' = 'No Transactions' (omitted); '(**)' = 'Less than absolute value of $500,000' (none in this section). Values as printed, thousands separators stripped, negatives as leading '-'. Nine-column model: 3 periods x (Gross Outlays / Applicable Receipts / Outlays[net]). Flat section: no printed bureau subtotals; the nine column roll-ups sum all lines into Total--Department of Justice. Three lines carry an Applicable Receipts value (Federal Prison System, Proprietary Receipts, Offsetting Governmental Receipts), so the Applicable column rolls up with three sources -- no single-source standalone is needed. Federal Prison System is the only line printing gross, applicable and net together, so it also carries the per-line net identity. Non-default tolerances quote the Table-5 rounding note (p. 23): 'Note: Details may not add to totals due to rounding.'",
